course: dictionary
lesson: 13214
title: Formal words and their parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound grown-up because they belong to formal writing, such as rules, letters and laws. Furtherance is one of them. It means the act of helping something to move forward or succeed. «The school was built in furtherance of the children's learning.» The building helps learning move forward.
explain: Look inside the word. Further means more forward, and the ending -ance turns it into a noun, a thing or an act. So furtherance is the act of pushing something forward. Once you spot further inside it, the meaning is easier to remember.
explain: Notice the phrase «in furtherance of». It is a set phrase, a group of words that always go together. When you see it, read it as "to help", and the rest of the sentence will make sense. «The club raised money in furtherance of the new library.» The club wanted the library to succeed.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The club raised money to help the new library move forward» means about the same, so you have found the right idea.
fact: Furtherance is a noun. It means the act of helping something move forward or succeed.
fact: «She practised every day in furtherance of her dream of becoming a doctor.» She practised to help that dream move forward.
fact: Furtherance is uncountable: you say "the furtherance of science", not "a furtherance" or "furtherances".
fact: It is mostly found in formal and legal writing, such as rules, letters and contracts.
fact: Further means more forward, and -ance is an ending that makes a noun.
exercise: «The volunteers met every week in furtherance of the park project.» What does furtherance mean in this sentence? | Stopping the project for good | Painting the gate red | A kind of park bench | *Helping the project move forward
exercise: «The charity was set up in furtherance of education.» What does in furtherance of education mean? | To stop children going to school | To pay for a new school bus | *To help education move forward | To make education more expensive
exercise: Which is the correct way to write it? | *the furtherance of science | furtherances of science | furthered of science | a furtherance of science
test: «The new rule was made in furtherance of safety on the roads.» What does this suggest? | *The rule was made to help safety move forward | The rule was made to ban safety | The rule was made as a funny joke | The rule was made by accident
test: What is the best way to check the meaning of furtherance? | *Swap in "helping something move forward" and see if the sentence still makes sense | Look only at the first letter | Count the letters and guess | Guess that it is a type of bird
exam: Which parts of the word make furtherance easier to work out? | It rhymes with a bird, so it must be a bird | Fur means animal hair, and -ther means small | It is a short word, so it must mean small | *Further means forward, and -ance makes a noun
